## Concrete next work

The private full-size coordinator already exists. Next local implementation
should wire a versioned fixed full-size guardian/entry around it, reusing
the resource, kernel-I/O and input-mount components. Preserve the qualified
tiny synthetic entry and the old public runner's unconditional rejection.

That integration must bind actual host/runtime identity, immutable backing or
excluded external writers, exact input ownership and recursive read-only mount
readback, fresh exclusive output, independent PID/cgroup supervision and native
resource enforcement. Read-only binds do not prove source immutability, and a
filesystem quota is not cumulative write accounting. Current cooperative
content ledgers do not prove arbitrary native writes are metered.

No host is selected or admitted. No full-size adapter is yet admitted, resource
or transfer budget approved, or S3 input acquired. Gate 5, real import,
training authorization and production eligibility remain incomplete/false.
No GPU needs to be turned on for this local integration work. All five files
created in this step remain local and unpushed.
